## Sign-in

{% if definition.auth.password %}
The users sign in on `/sign-in` with a user name and a password. Set
`AUTH_SECRET` to a long random text. With `SEED_PASSWORD`, the seed
gives each seed user this password.
{% else %}
The users sign in on `/sign-in` with a provider. Set `AUTH_SECRET` to a
long random text.
{% endif %}
{% if definition.auth.providers %}
The sign-in page has a button for each OpenID Connect provider: the
authorization code flow with PKCE. Register the redirect URI
`<PUBLIC_URL>/auth/providers/<name>/callback` at each provider, and set
`PUBLIC_URL` to the URL of the app for the browsers.

| Provider | Issuer | Client ID | Client secret |
| -------- | ------ | --------- | ------------- |
{% for name, p in definition.auth.providers.items() %}
| `{{ name }}` | `{{ name | upper }}_ISSUER` (default `{{ p.issuer }}`) | `{{ p.client_id_env }}` | `{{ p.client_secret_env }}` |
{% endfor %}
{% endif %}
{% if definition.auth.sign_up %}
New users make an account on `/sign-up`.
{% endif %}
{% if definition.auth.sign_up and definition.auth.sign_up.verify_email %}
A new user confirms the email address before the first sign-in: the
app sends a message with a link to `/verify-email`. The link is valid
for {{ definition.auth.sign_up.verify_email.token_minutes }} minutes.
{% endif %}
{% if definition.auth.password_reset %}
A user who forgets the password asks for a reset link on
`/forgot-password`. The link opens `/reset-password`, and is valid for
{{ definition.auth.password_reset.token_minutes }} minutes and one time.
{% endif %}
{% if definition.auth.password_reset or (definition.auth.sign_up and definition.auth.sign_up.verify_email) %}
Write the delivery of the messages (for example an email) in
`src/shared/auth/messages.ext.ts`. Until then, with
`ENVIRONMENT=development`, the app writes the links to the log. Set
`PUBLIC_URL` to the URL of the app for the browsers: the links use it.
{% endif %}
{% endif %}

